On Radix, `ls` leaves out of a directory's listing the names its
`.hidden` file lists, one a line, as GNOME Files and Nemo do, unless -a
or -A asks for every name. Dukovo's root holds the Unix names of its
folders (/bin, /dev, /etc, /proc and the rest) as links to the plainly
named ones, and its `.hidden` lists them, so that `ls /` shows only
folders a reader can make sense of (ADR 0113). Dukovo only.

